ACKNOWLEDGMENTS
The Government of the Republic of the Marshall Islands would like to thank and acknowledge the 
households and individuals who participated in and provided key information collected the 2021 
Population and Housing Census. It would also like to thank and acknowledge the Supervisors and 
Enumerators for their essential role in interviewing households. The 2021 Census was implemented 
by the Economic Policy, Planning and Statistics Office (EPPSO). All staff of EPPSO are acknowledged 
for their important role in the survey, with particular mention to Fred de Brum, Scott Keju, Joyceline 
Mellan–Kattil and John Henry. 
This document was compiled by the Statistics for Development Division of SPC and the EPPSO would like 
to thank and acknowledge the contributions from our partners. 
The Statistics for Development Division of the Pacific Community (SPC) is acknowledged for its role as lead 
technical agency supporting EPPSO throughout all phases of the Census, including questionnaire design, 
training, data processing and analysis and reporting. Michael Sharp, Scott Pontifex, Toga Raikoti, Peter 
Brueckmann and Luis de la Rua are acknowledged for their important input. 
We would also like express our appreciation to Asian Development Bank (ADB) local staff Ellen Paul and 
Denise Jack for their involvement in the data collection fieldwork and supervision. Support was also 
provided from UNFPA’s Pacific Sub-Regional Office in the development of this report and is warmly 
acknowledged. 
